Changes code from Helium's helium/core/add-native-bangs.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors).

Helium's !bangs come from its services (<services base>/bangs.json, behind consent). Ardia never turns the services
on, and its address bar is its own (packages/core), so Chromium's omnibox never uses bangs. LoadBangs now answers at
once with an empty catalogue whatever the prefs say: no loader is made, no retry is armed and nothing is requested.
The rest of the bangs code stays and compiles.

--- a/components/search_engines/template_url_bang_manager.cc
+++ b/components/search_engines/template_url_bang_manager.cc
@@ -184,13 +184,7 @@
   weak_ptr_factory_.InvalidateWeakPtrs();
   backoff_.Reset();
   callback_ = std::move(callback);
-
-  if (!helium::ShouldFetchBangs(*prefs_)) {
-    OnBangsLoaded(base::MakeRefCounted<Catalogue>(std::vector<Bang>()));
-    return;
-  }
-
-  StartFetch();
+  OnBangsLoaded(base::MakeRefCounted<Catalogue>(std::vector<Bang>()));
 }
 
 void BangManager::StartFetch() {
